#import "../template.typ": guide, guide-inline

= Background Information

#guide[
  *ABE Guideline:* Provide a short overview of the theory and scientific literature that is relevant for your thesis work, and necessary to understand the problem. The literature compiled here can be used and extended for the literature review chapter of your final thesis.

  *Tip:* This is not the full literature review — it is the foundation for one. Aim for 2–4 pages covering the key concepts, models, and prior work that a reader needs to follow your research questions and methods. Organise thematically (not chronologically) and cite properly throughout.
]

== Key Concepts and Definitions

#guide[
  *Hint:* Define the core technical or domain-specific terms your thesis relies on. For example, if your thesis involves machine learning in agriculture, briefly introduce the relevant ML paradigm (supervised learning, NLP, computer vision, etc.) and the agricultural concept it applies to (crop monitoring, pest detection, yield prediction, etc.). A reader from the other side of your interdisciplinary work should be able to follow.
]

== State of the Art

#guide[
  *Hint:* Summarise the most relevant recent work (last 5–10 years). What have others tried? What were their results and limitations? Where does the literature converge, and where are there contradictions or open questions? This sets up the gap your problem statement identified.

  *Tip:* Use a structured approach — consider organising by method, by crop/system, or by scale of application. Tables comparing prior studies (author, method, crop, key finding, limitation) work well here and can be reused in the thesis.
]

== Theoretical Framework

#guide[
  *Hint:* If your project builds on or extends a particular theoretical model, framework, or conceptual approach, describe it here. This might be an existing framework for technology adoption in agriculture (e.g., TAM, UTAUT), an agronomic model, or an engineering design methodology. Explain why this framework is appropriate for your research.
]
